Preheat oven to 350°F and lightly grease a #6-8-inch cast iron skillet{}.

Mix @butter{1/3%cup}(unsalted, melted), @brown sugar{1/3%cup}(packed) and @sugar{1/4%cup} with a spoon until combined.

Add in @egg yolk{1}, stirring quickly to incorporate.

Add @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup} + @all-purpose flour{2%tbsp}(fluffed and levelled), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp} and mix with a spoon until completely combined.

Stir in @chocolate chips{1/2%cup}(or chocolate chunks) and spread evenly into prepared skillet (if you like, throw some extra chocolate on top!).

Bake for ~{20-22%minutes} or until edges are crispy and center is just set.

Let cool slightly before topping with ice cream and serving.